<title>USA: HCC Insurance Holdings Inc Q3 shr $0.31.</title>
<headline>HCC Insurance Holdings Inc Q3 shr $0.31.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended September 30,	     1996	  1995</p>
<p> Total revenue				 35,569,000  31,535,000</p>
<p> Proforma net earnings (1)		 11,330,000   6,811,000</p>
<p> Proforma earnings per share (1)		 0.31	  0.19</p>
<p> Operating earnings after tax	    10,261,000   6,913,000</p>
<p> Operating earnings per share		    0.29	  0.20</p>
<p> Net earnings				  11,330,000   5,636,000</p>
<p> Earnings per share				  0.31	  0.16</p>
<p> Weighted average shares outstanding   35,993,000  34,999,000</p>
<p> Nine Months Ended September 30,	     1996	   1995</p>
<p> Total revenue			     110,882,000   92,209,000</p>
<p> Proforma net earnings (1)		31,041,000   19,027,000</p>
<p> Proforma earnings per share (1)		0.87	   0.60</p>
<p> Operating earnings after tax	   28,608,000   18,810,000</p>
<p> Operating earnings per share		   0.80	   0.59</p>
<p> Net earnings (2)			   16,734,000   15,990,000</p>
<p> Earnings per share (2)			   0.47	   0.50</p>
<p> Weighted average shares outstanding  35,823,000   31,828,000</p>
<p>(1) Proforma adjustments have been made: a) to 1995 figures to reflect comparable compensation expense to LDG officers; b) to 1995 and 1996 figures to reflect appropriate income tax expense despite LDG's S Corporation (non-taxable) status prior to reorganization and merger with the company; and c) to 1996 figures to eliminate merger related expenses and the non-recurring compensation charge of $14.4 million (net of a $9.6 million income tax benefit) relating to the compensatory stock grant to certain key employees from LDG's majority shareholder.  </p>
<p>(2) Net for 1996 nine months reduced by merger related expenses of $2.1 million and a non-recurring compensation charge of $14.4 million (net of a $9.6 million income tax benefit) relating to the compensatory stock grant to certain key employees from LDG's majority shareholder or a total of $0.40 per share.</p>
